#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-edit.md:29
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-edit.md:31
msgid ""
"This command opens the Nix expression of a derivation in an editor. The "
"filename and line number of the derivation are taken from its "
"`meta.position` attribute. Nixpkgs' `stdenv.mkDerivation` sets this "
"attribute to the location of the definition of the `meta.description`, "
"`version` or `name` derivation attributes."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-edit.md:37
msgid ""
"The editor to invoke is specified by the `EDITOR` environment variable. It "
"defaults to `cat`. If the editor is `emacs`, `nano`, `vim` or `kak`, it is "
"passed the line number of the derivation using the argument `+<lineno>`."
msgstr ""

